{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1226009-what-unknown-uplifted-races-do-you-think-there","id":1226009,"title":"What Unknown Uplifted Races do you think there?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-08T19:44:47-07:00","id":1226009,"title":"What Unknown Uplifted Races do you think there?","content":"So we already have an idea of three other uplifted races that has been mentioned in the material. Rats, Badgers, and Lizards. We also have a small inkling on how they are like on a societal level as well or at least we have ideas. That said these three certainly aren't the last of the uplifted races we can see in the future, but it's beginning. So here's a question. What other animals do you think will show up in the world of pugmire, and to add a little bit more to that. How do you envision there society to appear like. Whether super detailed or through stereotypes by the other races. Just thought this be a fun thing to ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T08:37:28-07:00","id":1226091,"title":"","content":"ferrets, ferrets would be nice, some sort of bird - parrot or corvid would be good, not sure how i would characterise any of these though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T11:43:53-07:00","id":1226104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1226009-what-unknown-uplifted-races-do-you-think-there?p=1226091#post1226091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ferrets, ferrets would be nice, some sort of bird - parrot or corvid would be good, not sure how i would characterise any of these though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The badgers include not only their namesake species, but also otters, weasels, ferrets, polecats and wolverines, per the Pugmire core (p. 132).<br /> <br /> It also mentions there're fish and birds as well (p. 131).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T11:52:31-07:00","id":1226105,"title":"","content":"I'd write something about swine, mainly channelling my love for George Orwell's Animal Farm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T12:52:52-07:00","id":1226120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1226009-what-unknown-uplifted-races-do-you-think-there?p=1226105#post1226105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd write something about swine, mainly channelling my love for George Orwell's Animal Farm.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Communist pigs. Well that would be interesting in one way or another","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T01:13:36-07:00","id":1226216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1226009-what-unknown-uplifted-races-do-you-think-there?p=1226105#post1226105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd write something about swine, mainly channelling my love for George Orwell's Animal Farm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huzzah for Pigmire! The only game where nobody cares if your character is a complete boar!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T15:40:54-07:00","id":1226309,"title":"","content":"In the Cats/Dogs argument, I tend to vote for Reptiles, so I'm really hoping to see more on the lizard races. My ideal Pugmire PC is a big fat iguana-dude with a frilly mohawk and a relic surfboard! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1226009-what-unknown-uplifted-races-do-you-think-there?p=1226216#post1226216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huzzah for Pigmire! The only game where nobody cares if your character is a complete boar!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I want to get in on the pun action too! Don't hog it all, White Oak Dragon! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T17:11:29-07:00","id":1226334,"title":"","content":"I would really love it if the currently defined Uplifted species were to get their own books. I feel like I'm getting kind of worried that it won't happen. Rats with their Science! and pseudo psionics on one hand and Italian crime families on the other are exciting to me. I'm getting an almost Arabian Nights vibe from the Lizard NPCs we're seeing, and there's so much to explore there. And then there's the Mustelids we seem to naturally think of as the 'weasel family' that we're calling Badgers for some reason. At first blush they seem like the Orcs of the setting but I'd almost give them a pre-Roman Celt feel. I feel like Rats would almost have the best chance to be the next thing just because they don't necessarily need a *new* slice of the map laid out for them. On the other hand Badgers actually already have the six 'divisions' already laid out from the Pugmire book. Still, I'd love for some Lizard action.<br /> <br /> If I had to guess a future unreferenced Uplifted species I'd have to guess Birds. Feels like Apes are right out, but Birds seem to make sense and you could get some great divisions within them, from your Songbirds to your Raptors to your Mimics to your Carrion-eaters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T13:23:48-07:00","id":1238042,"title":"","content":"If there would be some Birds Kingdom, it need to be stated as been raided by previous Kingdoms of Cats that now are Monarchies of Mau. Today I was in my partner's parents house and his mother cat greeted us with small bird she killed and brought to her kittens - very proud of her deed and teachings younglings. Probably now Monarchies are above so much bloodshed - like from the end of Cats and Dogs War - but animosities and history should reflects Cats predatory instincts against Birds.<br /> <br /> As to model of Birds Kingdom - I think best would be Medieval France - with many fiefdoms, divided by nobles - or some Haitan/Croel mix of indegious tribes with 'high European' cultures. Something like that. Birds are 'colorful', in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T05:57:22-07:00","id":1238563,"title":"","content":"I'm just sitting here picturing the amazing hairdo my buffalo character could have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T06:21:21-07:00","id":1238569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AutoDefenestrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1226009-what-unknown-uplifted-races-do-you-think-there?p=1226334#post1226334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would really love it if the currently defined Uplifted species were to get their own books. I feel like I'm getting kind of worried that it won't happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you're going to be happy with at least one of our Gen Con announcements, then.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T12:27:10-07:00","id":1240166,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d love it if there was a country modeled on Edo Japan to the degree Pugmire is on Feudal England, with Foxes and Racoon Dogs. Make corvids (Tengu) and turtles (kappa) the hostile outsiders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-30-2018, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:58:22-07:00","id":1241425,"title":"","content":"An undersea empire of fish. . .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Hosting <a href=\"http://opx-finalfrontier.wikidot.com\" target=\"_blank\">Outpost Phoenix</a>, an Non-Affiliated, Live-Action Star Trek <a href=\"https://discord.gg/6zwnyzm\" target=\"_blank\">Discord</a> Sim. New players are always welcome!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11235-arzie","name":"Arzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T16:08:01-07:00","id":1242112,"title":"","content":"A mix of Hamsters, Armadillos and maybe some birds (Parrots, Toucans, Quetzal) and exotic amphibians (tree frogs, axlotl, etc), the society modeled mostly after Central and South American pre-Columbian native cultures, with a few colonial touches that would likely be close to a Spanish Creole version of what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> suggested for the fiefdoms in his last post. I'd like that a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T18:06:30-07:00","id":1242166,"title":"","content":"In theory, I think ANY creature could be uplifted, and I'm sure there'll be plenty of homebrew uplifts cause someone at table X loves goldfish, and someone at table Y loves horses, and someone at table Z loves kangaroos.<br /> <br /> Now that's all well and good and perfectly fine, and maybe in 10 years we'll have quite a few source books on other uplifts, and there will still be no reason not to have some custom uplifts at your table cause that's the game you want<br /> <br /> I think it would be nice to know more about how the uplifts were chosen, but no need to put too fine a point of the mystery of the world either. not for some time at least. It could be some scientist or group knew mankind was on it's way out and had little time to preserve..., well, not &quot;humanity&quot; but intelligent life on earth and quick and dirty, started the Uplift of what was at hand, cats, rats, and dogs, and it took some number of generations and that's about all there is, but with some fallout that generated the monsters too. Or it could have been intelligence based, and pets, if not all those in the wild at least started uplifting once the cause was released, so new uplifts could always appear over time, and/or maybe in just certain areas.<br /> <br /> Maybe old world zoos are isolated cosmopolitan communities?<br /> <br /> I think pretty much anything could be uplifted, but if everything is uplifted, it's not gonna be as special being uplifted, but no reason it has to be just the dogs, cats, and rats that are known right now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24473-willowfang","name":"Willowfang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T06:55:52-07:00","id":1247369,"title":"","content":"In <a href=\"https://onyxpathcast.podbean.com/e/episode-15-gen-con-2018-retrospective/\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Pathcast 15</a> ( around time 14:00 of audition ), <b>Eddy Fate</b> mentioned that there is problem with imaging how should Uplifted Birds physiology looks like \u2013 especially hands and feet. If I may advise something as a fan, I would point not to evolution, but to <i>devolution</i> of the species in question. Particularly, that all Birds comes from common ancestor <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archaeopteryx\" target=\"_blank\">Archaeopteryx</a> that had gripping hands and feet. I think most of Uplifted Birds can easily take inspirations from this species anatomy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/624/media/images/75003000/jpg/_75003400_e4450111-artwork_of_an_archaeopteryx,_the_first_bird-spl.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/624/media/images/75003000/jpg/_75003400_e4450111-artwork_of_an_archaeopteryx,_the_first_bird-spl.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.dinosaurjungle.com/focus_archaeopteryx.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://www.dinosaurjungle.com/focus_archaeopteryx.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T08:11:00-07:00","id":1247384,"title":"","content":"Or also, this really isn't a case of sudden evolution or punctuated equilibrium. Somehow they got the term &quot;Uplifted, which to me suggests the initial races were genetically altered. If they weren't altered and didn't coexist with man, they couldn't possibly have the idea or any code of a &quot;Good Boy&quot; passed down through oral tradition<br /> <br /> So while some different version could be written, I would say mankind genetically altered the races they did, which means (just about) anything goes<br /> <br /> So I would say all the humanoid races in Pugmire only have two breasts/nipples<br /> <br /> Winged humanoids have wings on their back and arms in the usual humanoid places<br /> <br /> Eyes are a little more forward for binocular vision where they could otherwise be more to the sides<br /> <br /> And other differences that would make them a little more human-like in function wherever a more fluid transition might be a bit problematic to a human condition, like more than 2 breasts, or non-forward vision, and prolly dozens of other little things that could make a body wear out prematurely, like head turning to look forward, over stressed muscle development if an arm had to flap to fly, as well as being big and strong enough to lift heavy loads<br /> <br /> It could even be that birds lose their wings to have arms, but I don't think we, or anyone would want to use that idea of &quot;realism&quot;. I'd rather they have wings and not lose that bit of flavor myself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24473,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24473-willowfang","user":"Willowfang","date":". 08-19-2018, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24473-willowfang","name":"Willowfang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T21:07:56-07:00","id":1252110,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't like the idea of having every animal under the sun &quot;uplifted&quot;. If I'd wanted to play a generic anthropomorphic RPG I'd play Ironclaw.<br /> Parties of dogs and cats are alright, but not dogs and cats and mice and rabbits and ducks and moose and squirrel...<br /> <br /> I'm not even partial to birds in general, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24594-lightjammer","name":"lightjammer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T05:16:39-07:00","id":1252726,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to leave this here...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/article_25887_6-animals-with-jobs-more-impressive-than-yours.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cracked.com/article_25887...han-yours.html</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T16:08:03-07:00","id":1253405,"title":"","content":"Snakes... snakes are uplifted.<br /> <br /> In their culture, the term <i>&quot;slap on the wrist&quot;</i> is replaced with <i>&quot;boop on the snoot&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}